# S10 — /summary + periodic group digest (live-e2e Phase 1 scenario 10,
# M1-546). Both replies are progress-notified: the final body arrives via an
# item EDIT (chatItemUpdated), exercising the finalized-union observation path.
# Timeouts are generous — llama.cpp on 4 vCPU takes 60-120 s for prose
# (HANDOFF §Live-run notes).
#
# Host preconditions: seeded READY corpus (prod/live-seed.sh) and 'admin' has
# followed sources/tags so the summary window is non-empty; group 'live-group'
# approved with digests enabled; the digest window config-aimed at wall-clock
# now (D-live-8: morning/evening-slot-hour + window-width-minutes) BEFORE this
# scenario runs.

# 1. On-demand /summary: the finalized body carries bare source URLs — the
#    deterministic post set rendered (progress placeholders carry none).
send dm admin /summary -w 24h
expect substring 240000 http

# 2. Periodic group digest: the digest fires on the config-aimed window, not
#    in reply to this send — the send only opens the observation window; its
#    own toggle reply ("Periodic digest resumed…"/"already on") contains no
#    URL, so the expect can only be satisfied by the digest body. Last step,
#    widest timeout.
send group live-group admin @bot /digest on
expect substring 300000 http
